9. Requests the Analytical Support and Sanctions Monitoring Team established pursuant to resolution 1526 (2004) to submit, within 180 days of the adoption of this resolution, a special comprehensive report to the Security Council and its Committee established pursuant to resolutions 1267 (1999), 1989 (2011), and 2253 (2015) on the transnational external threat posed by ISIL-Khorasan, assessing its command structure, external operations networks, financing channels, and exploitation of emerging technologies;

10. Directs the Counter-Terrorism Committee Executive Directorate (CTED), in coordination with the United Nations Office of Counter-Terrorism (UNOCT), to facilitate technical assistance and capacity-building for requesting Member States, particularly frontline States and developing countries in Africa and other affected regions, based on national ownership and priorities, to identify vulnerabilities, mobilize resources, and bolster capabilities in virtual asset regulation, border and maritime security, critical infrastructure protection, and the interdiction of illicit trafficking networks, while ensuring full compliance with international human rights standards;

